RuntimeError: No module named 'sympy'

OlympiadBench scoring uses the official sympy symbolic judge, which needs `antlr4-python3-runtime==4.11` for sympy's parse_latex. That version conflicts with hydra-core/omegaconf (they pin 4.9.*), so it is NOT installed globally. Run scoring in an ephemeral uv env (no venv dir, no global change):
    uv run --no-project --with sympy --with 'antlr4-python3-runtime==4.11' \
        python scripts/eval_benchmark.py --benchmark olympiadbench --score-only
Predictions/extractions are cached, so you can generate them on the main env (optionally with --skip-extract) and re-run scoring via the uv command above. scripts/run_eval_all.sh already does this for you.
